data science work.

00:51:50.780 --> 00:51:52.570
- Yeah, we're a centralized

00:51:53.600 --> 00:51:55.610
function, a support
function really.

00:51:56.600 --> 00:52:00.620
And then more on a project
type basis would we consider

00:52:00.620 --> 00:52:03.080
ourselves embedded
with a team. So

00:52:05.300 --> 00:52:08.840
if we're working on a project
and we need to have the subject

00:52:08.840 --> 00:52:12.960
matter experts in the room,
then we're all in that way.

00:52:12.960 --> 00:52:14.135
So on a project basis

00:52:15.410 --> 00:52:19.640
maybe we would become embedded,
but we're never truly embedded

00:52:19.640 --> 00:52:22.680
because we don't
run the models and

00:52:23.900 --> 00:52:25.850
we're not really

00:52:27.230 --> 00:52:29.615
engaged in that rating process

00:52:30.230 --> 00:52:32.000
on the ground so much.

00:52:33.180 --> 00:52:34.220
So one thing, always

00:52:34.910 --> 00:52:37.310
quantitative and qualitative
part of the model--

00:52:37.850 --> 00:52:40.790
maybe I misspoke. I
meant like the rating

00:52:41.840 --> 00:52:43.310
process or the rating--

00:52:43.310 --> 00:52:44.230
the analysis

00:52:45.830 --> 00:52:47.435
is what I maybe
should have said.

00:52:48.010 --> 00:52:51.270
- I think we have time for
a few more questions here.

00:52:52.530 --> 00:52:54.720
But Allan, I see you had
