us are kind of familiar with conceptually--

00:53:18.140 --> 00:53:21.680
versus things that come into
your team from the businesses

00:53:21.680 --> 00:53:24.560
or from other customers. How
do you balance those things?

00:53:24.560 --> 00:53:27.665
What kind of help
do you have in picking

00:53:28.550 --> 00:53:30.320
when to do one
versus the other?

00:53:30.320 --> 00:53:30.820
- Yeah,

00:53:31.610 --> 00:53:32.600
I mean, this is

00:53:33.230 --> 00:53:38.450
getting back to that idea of
we employ some of the tools that

00:53:38.450 --> 00:53:43.010
are available to technology. So
we have a support mailbox,

00:53:43.010 --> 00:53:45.890
that's the quantitative
modeling support mailbox.

00:53:45.890 --> 00:53:48.800
So if somebody has a question
or something that they want us

00:53:48.800 --> 00:53:51.590
to work on, they send a--

00:53:51.590 --> 00:53:52.940
they send an email there.

00:53:52.940 --> 00:53:55.890
It automatically creates a
